@startuml Knock-Knock-TCP-Server-StateDiagram
title Knock Knock TCP Server - Conversation State Diagram for One Client

' State machine for a single client conversation

[*] --> WaitingForJokeRequest: Client connects

' ============================================================================
' WAITING FOR JOKE REQUEST STATE
' ============================================================================

state WaitingForJokeRequest {
	[*] --> SendPrompt: Entry
	SendPrompt --> SendPrompt: Server sends "Knock knock?"
	SendPrompt --> CheckJokeRequest: Read client message

	CheckJokeRequest --> SelectJoke: Client sends "joke"\n(case-insensitive)
	SelectJoke --> TransitionToWho: Use IJokeSelector strategy\nto pick a joke
	TransitionToWho --> WaitingForWho: Transition

	CheckJokeRequest --> SendError: Client sends\nanything else
	SendError --> SendError: Server sends "Please send\n'joke' to request\na knock knock joke."
	SendError --> CheckJokeRequest: Loop back waiting
}

' ============================================================================
' WAITING FOR "WHO'S THERE?" STATE
' ============================================================================

state WaitingForWho {
	[*] --> SendKnock: Entry
	SendKnock --> SendKnock: Server sends "Knock! Knock!"
	SendKnock --> CheckWho: Read client message

	CheckWho --> SendSetup: Client sends "Who's there?"\n(case-insensitive)
	SendSetup --> SendSetup: Server sends the joke's\n"Who" part
	SendSetup --> SendingPunchline: Transition

	CheckWho --> SendWhoError: Client sends\nanything else
	SendWhoError --> SendWhoError: Server sends "Please respond\nwith 'Who's there?'"
	SendWhoError --> CheckWho: Loop back waiting
}

' ============================================================================
' SENDING PUNCHLINE STATE
' ============================================================================

state SendingPunchline {
	[*] --> WaitForComplete: Entry
	WaitForComplete --> WaitForComplete: Read client message

	WaitForComplete --> SendPunchline: Any non-empty\nmessage received
	SendPunchline --> SendPunchline: Server sends the joke's\npunchline
	SendPunchline --> LoopOrExit: Transition

	WaitForComplete --> WaitForComplete: Empty message\n(wait for any input)
}

' ============================================================================
' LOOP OR EXIT STATE
' ============================================================================

state LoopOrExit {
	[*] --> AskMore: Entry
	AskMore --> AskMore: Server sends "Want another joke?\n(yes/no)"
	AskMore --> CheckResponse: Read client message

	CheckResponse --> LoopYes: Client sends "yes"\n(case-insensitive)
	CheckResponse --> LoopNo: Client sends "no"\n(case-insensitive)
	CheckResponse --> InvalidResponse: Client sends\nanything else

	LoopYes --> WaitingForJokeRequest: Transition to start new joke

	LoopNo --> Goodbye: Server sends "Thanks for\nchatting! Goodbye!"
	Goodbye --> [*]: Conversation ends\nClient thread exits

	InvalidResponse --> InvalidResponse: Server sends "Please respond\nwith 'yes' or 'no'."
	InvalidResponse --> CheckResponse: Loop back
}

' ============================================================================
' TRANSITIONS & NOTES
' ============================================================================

WaitingForJokeRequest --> WaitingForWho: Valid "joke" request
WaitingForWho --> SendingPunchline: Valid "Who's there?"
SendingPunchline --> LoopOrExit: Any non-empty message received
LoopOrExit --> WaitingForJokeRequest: "yes" response
LoopOrExit --> [*]: "no" response

' ============================================================================
' LEGEND & DOCUMENTATION
' ============================================================================

note bottom of WaitingForJokeRequest
  **Initial State**
  - Entry: Send "Knock knock?"
  - Valid input: "joke" (case-insensitive)
  - Invalid input: Loop with error message
  - Uses IJokeSelector strategy to select a joke
end note

note bottom of WaitingForWho
  **Setup Acknowledgment**
  - Entry: Send "Knock! Knock!"
  - Valid input: "Who's there?" (case-insensitive)
  - Invalid input: Loop with error message
end note

note bottom of SendingPunchline
  **Waiting for Prompt**
  - Entry: Wait for any non-empty message
  - Sends the joke's "Who" part
  - Then sends the punchline
  - Transitions to LoopOrExit
end note

note bottom of LoopOrExit
  **Conversation Continuation**
  - Asks: "Want another joke? (yes/no)"
  - Valid "yes": Loop back to initial state
  - Valid "no": Send goodbye and end conversation
  - Invalid input: Show error and re-ask
end note

note right of WaitingForJokeRequest, WaitingForWho, SendingPunchline, LoopOrExit
  All states handle disconnected clients gracefully.
  If the client disconnects, the state returns an error
  and the conversation thread terminates.
end note

@enduml
